Source: @DISTRO_ID@-base
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: @DISTRO_HOME_URL@
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: @DISTRO_ID@-base
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 @DISTRO_ID@-archive-keyring,
 @DISTRO_ID@-apt-source,
 linux-generic,
 initramfs-tools,
 grub-efi-amd64-signed,
 shim-signed,
 secureboot-db,
 efibootmgr,
 fwupd,
 fwupd-signed,
 cryptsetup-initramfs,
 systemd-sysv,
 udev,
 kmod,
 dbus-broker,
 dbus-user-session,
 libpam-systemd,
 polkitd,
 systemd-resolved,
 systemd-timesyncd,
 network-manager,
 wpasupplicant,
 wireless-regdb,
 netbase,
 iproute2,
 iputils-ping,
 ca-certificates,
 pipewire-audio,
 alsa-ucm-conf,
 alsa-topology-conf,
 firmware-sof-signed,
 apparmor,
 sudo,
 locales,
 tzdata,
 kbd,
 console-setup,
 less,
 e2fsprogs,
 dosfstools
Description: @DISTRO_NAME@ base system (metapackage)
 Everything a @DISTRO_NAME@ system needs to boot, reach the network and play
 sound, before any desktop: Ubuntu's signed kernel, shim and GRUB, systemd,
 AppArmor, NetworkManager with wpa_supplicant, PipeWire with WirePlumber,
 cryptsetup for an encrypted root, fwupd for firmware updates (with
 fwupd-signed, the Canonical-signed EFI program that applies UEFI capsule
 updates), and the @DISTRO_NAME@ apt repository.
 .
 This package also sets the system's identity and apt behaviour: it diverts
 /usr/lib/os-release so the system identifies as @DISTRO_NAME@, turns apt's
 Install-Recommends off, and hands every network interface to NetworkManager
 through netplan.
